SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] National Clean Energy Week - September 15 thr
 ough 19
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\,\nMaine is committed to advancing an affordable\, rel
 iable\, and cleaner energy future and enjoys abundant forms of renewable e
 nergy that power homes and businesses across the State\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nc
 lean energy sources including solar\, wind\, hydropower\, and biomass faci
 lities provide cost-effective power to Maine and the region\; and\nWHEREAS
 \,\nthe generation of power from renewable sources\, including forms such 
 as hydro\, wood\, wind\, and solar\, accounts for\n54 percent of net elect
 ricity generation in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nMaine has increased its Renew
 able Portfolio Standard to 90 percent by 2040 and adopted a complementary 
 Clean Energy Standard to reach 100 percent clean energy by 2040\; and\nWHE
 REAS\,\nMaine leads New England in wind-powered generation\, and ranks el
 eventh in the country in its share of electricity generated from wind\; an
 d\nWHEREAS\,\nin 2024\, hydroelectric power generated nearly 20 percent o
 f the electricity in Maine\, and Maine ranked ninth in the nation for hydr
 opower production as a share of total energy generated\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nM
 aine’s more than 16\,000 clean energy jobs grow local economies and boo
 st economic development\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nMaine has led the nation in the 
 adoption of high efficiency electric heat pumps\, installing more than 200
 \,000 units with a goal of 275\,000 installed by 2027\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nNa
 tional Clean Energy Week provides an opportunity for individuals\, local g
 overnments\, corporations\, and other organizations in Maine to champion c
 ommonsense solutions that address the United States’ evolving economic a
 nd energy needs\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\,\nbe it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mil
 ls\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim September 15-19\,
  2026\, as\nNational Clean Energy Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\, an
 d I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testimony whereof\
 , I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN
  under my\nhand at Augusta this seventeenth day of\nAugust Two Thousand Tw
 enty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamat
 ions/2026-08-national-clean-energy-week-september-15-through-19
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-national-clean-energy-week-september-15-through-19
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
